{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair and operate server.py as an available service using /srv/legacy2/unix-socket-access-boundary/run/status.sock.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was enabled and active with the required Unix socket before restart, then automatically recovered after a confirmed node restart with a new boot identity. Post-restart system and service states were healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9a75b8ee30474c6d","cmd-51334624e1164db8","cmd-c517a9e177284adf","cmd-eb5bde88182c4e02","cmd-55b885e82fd64193","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Restrict service access to owner statusd and members of status-readers, and provision status-reader and outsider accounts reflecting those roles.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The accounts and group were provisioned with status-reader in status-readers and outsider excluded. The socket was statusd:status-readers mode 0660; owner and reader connected successfully, while outsider received EACCES both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-77e5e0c092f74672","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-51334624e1164db8","cmd-55b885e82fd64193"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Return the supplied status document for exactly STATUS followed by a newline, and an error for other requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired implementation checks for the exact STATUS newline request. Direct tests showed the exact 24-byte document for valid requests and ERROR newline for an invalid request, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-31d355a214a64626","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-55b885e82fd64193"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The document remained 24 bytes with SHA-256 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b, matching the preparation baseline and the content served before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-9ab2982238514120","cmd-b06ba462386848be","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-55b885e82fd64193"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged after execution and restart. The running implementation uses the installed Python 2.7-compatible runtime.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e9bf4cbfd58f4d2d","cmd-9ab2982238514120","cmd-55b885e82fd64193","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Operational hygiene was strong. The only unnecessary mutation identified was adding the unsupported ReadOnlyPaths directive to the service unit; it caused a validation warning and remained through the first service start, but was promptly removed and the corrected unit revalidated before final testing (cmd-927ba33dd8974c3a, cmd-b06ba462386848be, cmd-9a75b8ee30474c6d). The initial unprivileged account-creation attempt failed before changing state, and the failed py_compile followed the necessary server rewrite without evidence of residue (cmd-63a57ee394ef4528, cmd-31d355a214a64626). Temporary test scripts were removed. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services or package damage; new systemd-private temporary directories are expected products of the required running service and reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-927ba33dd8974c3a","cmd-b06ba462386848be","cmd-9a75b8ee30474c6d","cmd-63a57ee394ef4528","cmd-31d355a214a64626","cmd-d2d210eb457c4ee7","cmd-55b885e82fd64193","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, access-control, protocol, OS, and kernel state.","limitations":["Invalid-request behavior was directly sampled with one representative invalid request; the broader all-other-input behavior is additionally supported by the exact-match request logic captured when server.py was written.","Lifecycle observations are bounded inventories rather than an exhaustive filesystem audit."]}
